 "text": "Hey! How are you feeling? Use plain language and stay calm. Say something like, the spice level is too high for me, could it be balanced? It' better not to do it right away. Waiting until after the dish looks like it' going helps it feel less like criticism and more like an honest question. They' likely used to it. Most places appreciate a polite word, especially when it helps the chef adjust the style. dramatic is over the top, but honest feedback is important. Just keep it short and focused on one thing, so it' easy to fix.",
